  "segments": [
    {
      "text": "A round manhole cover can do something surprisingly important:",
      "start": 0.071,
      "end": 3.09
    },
    {
      "text": "stay above the manhole.",
      "start": 3.475,
      "end": 4.529
    },
    {
      "text": "A circular cover cannot fall straight through its own circular opening.",
      "start": 4.881,
      "end": 8.222
    },
    {
      "text": "With some other shapes, orientation can become a problem.",
      "start": 8.537,
      "end": 11.18
    },
    {
      "text": "Round covers are also easy to roll, don't need to be rotated into one exact",
      "start": 11.561,
      "end": 15.865
    },
    {
      "text": "alignment, and fit naturally over circular shafts.",
      "start": 15.865,
      "end": 18.544
    },
    {
      "text": "So engineers didn't choose the circle because it looks nice. They chose a shape",
      "start": 18.887,
      "end": 22.56
    },
    {
      "text": "that quietly solves several annoying problems at once,",
      "start": 22.56,
      "end": 25.4
    },
    {
      "text": "which is basically engineering's favorite way of showing off.",
      "start": 25.703,
      "end": 28.204
    }
  ],
